1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:04,600
How a Japanese Greengrocer
Changed the Way Singapore Shops

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:09,406
When Yaohan opened at Plaza Singapura
on the 1st of November 1974,

3
00:00:09,486 --> 00:00:13,182
it put a supermarket, a
department store and a hall

4
00:00:13,262 --> 00:00:17,475
of ready-to-eat food under one
roof, with fixed price tags

5
00:00:17,555 --> 00:00:21,775
on everything and staff who
greeted shoppers at the door.

6
00:00:21,775 --> 00:00:25,300
Nothing in Singapore had
worked quite like it.

7
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:29,188
About a million people came
through in the first week,

8
00:00:29,268 --> 00:00:31,325
in a country of 2.2 million.

9
00:00:31,325 --> 00:00:36,264
Half a century on, the stores that
followed Yaohan in have mostly closed,

10
00:00:36,344 --> 00:00:39,220
and Yaohan itself no
longer exists anywhere

11
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,382
near Singapore — but the
idea it arrived with,

12
00:00:42,462 --> 00:00:47,000
good food sold cheaply in the
basement, has outlasted all of them.

13
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,451
Yaohan began in 1930 as a
single fruit-and-vegetable

14
00:00:51,531 --> 00:00:54,239
shop in Atami, a hot-spring town

15
00:00:54,319 --> 00:00:58,675
south-west of Tokyo, run
by Ryohei and Katsu Wada.

16
00:00:58,675 --> 00:01:03,844
Their son Kazuo Wada built it into
a supermarket chain in Shizuoka

17
00:01:03,924 --> 00:01:08,536
prefecture and then, from the
early 1970s, took it abroad —

18
00:01:08,616 --> 00:01:14,023
first to Brazil in 1971, then
Singapore in 1974, and later Hong Kong,

19
00:01:14,103 --> 00:01:18,875
Malaysia, Brunei, Thailand,
Indonesia and the United States.

20
00:01:18,875 --> 00:01:21,506
At its height the group ran

21
00:01:21,586 --> 00:01:25,000
around 450 stores in 16 countries.

22
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:29,630
Wada was a member of Seicho-no-Ie,
a Japanese spiritual movement,

23
00:01:29,710 --> 00:01:35,572
and new Yaohan recruits in Japan were
expected to join it and attend its seminars;

24
00:01:35,652 --> 00:01:39,275
the requirement was applied
more loosely overseas.

25
00:01:39,275 --> 00:01:42,193
The Singapore company was a joint venture

26
00:01:42,273 --> 00:01:45,125
with the Development Bank of Singapore.

27
00:01:45,125 --> 00:01:49,204
Its Plaza Singapura store
opened with sixteen supermarket

28
00:01:49,284 --> 00:01:53,363
checkouts and nineteen
department-store counters and was,

29
00:01:53,443 --> 00:01:57,675
at the time, the largest store
of its kind in the country.

30
00:01:57,675 --> 00:02:01,139
Until Yaohan, a Singaporean
buying groceries went

31
00:02:01,219 --> 00:02:03,743
to a wet market or a provision shop,

32
00:02:03,823 --> 00:02:08,525
and buying clothes or household
goods meant somewhere else again.

33
00:02:08,525 --> 00:02:11,951
Yaohan put all of it
together, added a food section

34
00:02:12,031 --> 00:02:15,732
selling cooked dishes to take
away, and printed a price

35
00:02:15,812 --> 00:02:19,250
on every item so there was
nothing to haggle over.

36
00:02:19,250 --> 00:02:21,700
The format spread quickly.

37
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:26,521
Yaohan opened at Katong in
1977, Thomson Plaza in 1979,

38
00:02:26,601 --> 00:02:32,403
Bukit Timah Plaza in 1981, and
Jurong and Parkway Parade in 1983 —

39
00:02:32,483 --> 00:02:38,275
moving out of the centre and into
the housing estates as it went.

40
00:02:38,275 --> 00:02:40,600
It also had company.

41
00:02:40,600 --> 00:02:44,948
Isetan had reached Singapore
two years ahead of Yaohan,

42
00:02:45,028 --> 00:02:49,214
opening in 1972 in the Apollo
Hotel on Havelock Road,

43
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:53,400
the first Japanese department
store in the country.

44
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:57,725
Daimaru anchored Liang Court from 1983.

45
00:02:57,725 --> 00:03:01,975
Sogo opened at Raffles City in 1986.

46
00:03:01,975 --> 00:03:05,714
Takashimaya arrived last and largest,

47
00:03:05,794 --> 00:03:08,375
at Ngee Ann City in 1993.

48
00:03:08,375 --> 00:03:12,159
For roughly two decades the
Japanese department store was

49
00:03:12,239 --> 00:03:16,431
the template for a Singapore
shopping centre: a big-name anchor

50
00:03:16,511 --> 00:03:20,973
over several floors, a supermarket
and a food hall in the basement,

51
00:03:21,053 --> 00:03:24,375
and a fixed-price,
well-staffed floor in between.

52
00:03:24,375 --> 00:03:27,125
The retailers had reasons to be there —

53
00:03:27,205 --> 00:03:30,609
a maturing home market
in Japan, money to spend,

54
00:03:30,689 --> 00:03:34,825
and a Southeast Asian middle
class that was growing fast.

55
00:03:34,825 --> 00:03:39,496
By 1990 Kazuo Wada had decided
the company's future was in China,

56
00:03:39,576 --> 00:03:44,977
and he moved the group's base to Hong
Kong to run the expansion from there,

57
00:03:45,057 --> 00:03:49,150
listing the international arm
on the Hong Kong exchange.

58
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:52,723
The plans were enormous —
a thousand stores in China,

59
00:03:52,803 --> 00:03:55,824
and a flagship in Shanghai
that was, briefly,

60
00:03:55,904 --> 00:03:59,350
one of the largest department
stores in the world.

61
00:03:59,350 --> 00:04:03,591
The group borrowed heavily
to build them and was thinly

62
00:04:03,671 --> 00:04:08,150
capitalised when the 1997
Asian financial crisis arrived.

63
00:04:08,150 --> 00:04:11,629
On the 18th of September 1997 Yaohan's

64
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:16,873
Japanese parent filed for
protection from its creditors,

65
00:04:16,953 --> 00:04:19,575
owing about 161 billion yen.

66
00:04:19,575 --> 00:04:22,317
It was the biggest failure the Japanese

67
00:04:22,397 --> 00:04:25,075
retail sector had seen since the war.

68
00:04:25,075 --> 00:04:28,476
The national operations
were sold off in pieces:

69
00:04:28,556 --> 00:04:34,133
the Japanese stores went to the Aeon
group, the Hong Kong stores became Jusco,

70
00:04:34,213 --> 00:04:38,629
and the American stores were
bought by their own managers and,

71
00:04:38,709 --> 00:04:41,900
from 1998, rebranded
as Mitsuwa Marketplace.

72
00:04:41,900 --> 00:04:44,412
Yaohan's Singapore stores,

73
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:49,575
already unprofitable, closed
through 1997 and 1998.

74
00:04:49,575 --> 00:04:52,775
Yaohan was not the only one to leave.

75
00:04:52,775 --> 00:04:56,504
Sogo went into judicial
management in Singapore

76
00:04:56,584 --> 00:04:59,825
and shut its Raffles City store in 2000.

77
00:04:59,825 --> 00:05:05,325
Daimaru closed at Liang Court
in 2003 after twenty years.

78
00:05:05,325 --> 00:05:10,668
Isetan held on longer but has been
closing one store after another —

79
00:05:10,748 --> 00:05:15,293
Jurong in 2020, Katong in 2022,
the Serangoon and Tampines

80
00:05:15,373 --> 00:05:20,396
outlets more recently — and by
the end of 2025 was down from six

81
00:05:20,476 --> 00:05:25,500
stores in 2013 to essentially
one, its flagship on Scotts Road.

82
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:29,733
Of the department stores that
defined Orchard Road in the

83
00:05:29,813 --> 00:05:34,198
1980s and 1990s, only Takashimaya
still trades in something

84
00:05:34,278 --> 00:05:38,132
close to its original form,
held up by its location,

85
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:42,450
its size, and a year-round
calendar of fairs and events.

86
00:05:42,450 --> 00:05:45,675
What did carry through is the basement.

87
00:05:45,675 --> 00:05:50,344
The Japanese term is depachika —
the department-store food hall,

88
00:05:50,424 --> 00:05:55,025
stacked with prepared dishes,
bento, bakery and deli counters.

89
00:05:55,025 --> 00:05:58,305
Takashimaya's food hall
on Basement 2 is still

90
00:05:58,385 --> 00:06:01,373
one of the busiest places in the building,

91
00:06:01,453 --> 00:06:05,325
and Isetan's basement is
still where its shoppers go.

92
00:06:05,325 --> 00:06:10,542
The clearest sign of how durable
the idea is came in December 2017,

93
00:06:10,622 --> 00:06:14,100
when Don Don Donki opened
at Orchard Central:

94
00:06:14,180 --> 00:06:19,556
a 24-hour Japanese store built around
cheap, good, ready-to-eat food,

95
00:06:19,636 --> 00:06:24,775
which is close to what Yaohan
brought to Plaza Singapura in 1974.

96
00:06:24,775 --> 00:06:28,000
It now has outlets across the island.

97
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,675
Yaohan itself did not vanish completely.

98
00:06:31,675 --> 00:06:35,720
Its American stores live on
as Mitsuwa, its Macau store

99
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:39,920
still trades as New Yaohan,
and a shopper who moved from

100
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:44,045
Singapore to a Chicago suburb
could walk into a Mitsuwa

101
00:06:44,125 --> 00:06:48,325
today and be standing in what
was, until 1998, a Yaohan.

102
00:06:48,325 --> 00:06:51,618
Where it fits in the bigger
story: the shape of an

103
00:06:51,698 --> 00:06:56,003
ordinary Singapore mall — a
department store over several floors,

104
00:06:56,083 --> 00:06:58,837
groceries and a food hall in the basement,

105
00:06:58,917 --> 00:07:02,345
a fixed price on everything
— was a Japanese import,

106
00:07:02,425 --> 00:07:06,675
arriving with a company that then
bet itself on China and lost.

107
00:07:06,675 --> 00:07:09,750
The stores are nearly all gone.

108
00:07:09,750 --> 00:07:13,381
The habit they taught, of
going downstairs for something

109
00:07:13,461 --> 00:07:16,575
good to eat, is stronger
than it has ever been.
